{
  "id": "budapest-gambit",
  "name": "Budapest Gambit",
  "color": "black",
  "status": "draft",
  "summary": "Against the queen-pawn opening, Black gives a pawn for fast piece play, then wins it back with active knights and a bishop check.",
  "goal": {
    "title": "Give a pawn for quick piece play, then win it back",
    "text": "Black lets White keep an extra pawn at first. In return Black's pieces jump out fast: a knight attacks the extra pawn from the edge of the board, the other knight joins it, and a bishop comes out with check. Within a few moves Black wins the pawn back and enjoys the more active pieces.",
    "plans": [
      "Attack the extra white pawn with a knight from the edge of the board, and bring the other knight to help.",
      "Give a check with the dark-squared bishop to drag White's pieces onto awkward squares.",
      "Put the queen next to the king to add pressure on the same pawn.",
      "Take the pawn back as soon as it is safe, then castle."
    ],
